WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.390
An investor selling a
Put Option receives

2
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:20.065
a fixed premium and gives
another investor the right,

3
00:00:20.065 --> 00:00:21.655
but not the obligation,

4
00:00:21.655 --> 00:00:23.380
to sell an asset at

5
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.830
a predetermined price,
until expiration.

6
00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.100
A short put strategy
might be considered by

7
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.900
a risk-tolerant trader with

8
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.909
the opinion that a stock's price,

9
00:00:33.909 --> 00:00:36.250
is likely to increase and

10
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.030
or volatility is
likely to decrease.

11
00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:42.430
The put seller benefits from

12
00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:45.660
the passage of time and
the decreasing dividends.

13
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:48.800
The maximum gain is
the premium received,

14
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.760
which occurs at any price
above the strike price.

15
00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:55.580
The gain diminishes
as the price of the

16
00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.595
underlying falls below
the strike price.

17
00:00:58.595 --> 00:01:00.830
Break-even occurs at the sum of

18
00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.225
the strike price less
the premium received.

19
00:01:04.225 --> 00:01:06.210
Any price below that,

20
00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.735
the short put seller
begins to lose money,

21
00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:12.335
penny for penny, as the
underlying price decreases.

22
00:01:12.335 --> 00:01:15.050
Loss potential is substantial.

23
00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:17.720
Short put sellers must
ensure that they are

24
00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:22.490
sufficiently capitalized to
deliver any required shares.